course: dictionary
lesson: 6812
title: One word, many decorations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ornament is a small object that makes a room, a shelf or a Christmas tree look nice. It is not for a practical job. Families hang ornaments, also called baubles, on the tree, and grandparents often have a china ornament on the shelf.
explain: Ornament can also be a verb, meaning to decorate. «Ten courtiers ornamented with diamonds» means the courtiers were decorated with diamonds. The clue is the word «with», which tells you what the decoration is made of.
explain: In music, an ornament is extra notes added to decorate a tune. The tune is still there, but it is dressed up. When you meet ornament, ask: is this a thing, an action, or a part of music? The words around it will tell you.
fact: An ornament is a small object for decoration, not for a practical use.
fact: To ornament something is to decorate it.
fact: «Ornamented» means decorated with something, such as «ornamented with hearts».
fact: «A richly ornamented robe» means a robe with lots of rich decoration on it.
fact: In music, an ornament is extra notes added to decorate a tune.
exercise: «The shelf held a china ornament shaped like a bird.» What is an ornament here? | A real bird that can sing | A kind of shelf | A tool for cutting wood | * A small object for decoration
exercise: In «ten courtiers ornamented with diamonds», what does ornamented mean? | Broken | Hungry | * Decorated | Lost
exercise: What is an ornament in music? | A tune played twice | A loud drum beat | A torn sheet of music | * Extra notes added to decorate a tune
test: Dad says, «We will ornament the tree tonight.» What does ornament mean? | To wrap in paper | To water | * To decorate | To cut down
test: The Bible note says «richly ornamented robe». What does it mean? | A robe with no colours | * A robe decorated with rich decoration | A robe that is old and torn | A robe for swimming
exam: Nadia asks, "Does ornament only mean a Christmas bauble?" What is the answer? | Yes, it only ever means a Christmas bauble | No, it means something broken | * No, it can also mean decoration on a building or extra notes in a tune | Yes, it is only ever a verb
